<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Reversing a derivative</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Find each indefinite integral. Use \(c\) for the constant of integration.</p><p>(a)</p><div>\(\displaystyle \int {@kk@}\,dx =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b)</p><div>\(\displaystyle \int {@qq*x@}\,dx =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c)</p><div>\(\displaystyle \int {@pp*x^nn@}\,dx =\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Integration undoes differentiation: raise the power of \(x\) by \(1\) and divide by the new power, \(\int x^n\,dx = \dfrac{x^{n+1}}{n+1} + c\). A constant \(k\) is \(k x^0\), so it integrates to \(kx\).</p><p>(a) \(\displaystyle \int {@kk@}\,dx = {@F1@} + c\). Check: \(\dfrac{d}{dx}\left({@F1@} + c\right) = {@kk@}\).</p><p>(b) \(\displaystyle \int {@qq*x@}\,dx = \frac{ {@qq@}x^2}{2} + c = {@F2@} + c\). Check: \(\dfrac{d}{dx}\left({@F2@} + c\right) = {@qq*x@}\).</p><p>(c) \(\displaystyle \int {@pp*x^nn@}\,dx = \frac{ {@pp@}x^{ {@nn+1@} } }{ {@nn+1@} } + c = {@F3@} + c\). Check: \(\dfrac{d}{dx}\left({@F3@} + c\right) = {@pp*x^nn@}\).</p><p>Differentiating a constant gives \(0\), so we cannot tell which constant was there: write \(+\,c\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
